Literacy
Figure 5.1 shows that the literacy rate of the household population 10 years and older has increased from 97 
percent in the 1999 census to 98 percent in the 2011 census. While slightly more females were literate than 
males in 1999, this gap has reduced to almost nil in 2011. These figures are comparable, because in each census 
a literate person was defined as one who can, with understanding, both read and write a simple message in any 
one language.
 
